Description: A design-aware workflow for response surface methodology with two or more
    quantitative factors. The package integrates response-surface fitting, diagnostics of
    non-orthogonal and imperfect designs, canonical analysis, steepest ascent/descent,
    ridge analysis, constrained and global optimization, genetic algorithms, uncertainty
    quantification for optima, near-optimal regions, multiple-response desirability and
    Pareto analysis, design augmentation, economic optimum calculations, and static or
    interactive graphics. It additionally supports two-factor generalized response surfaces
    using generalized linear models, two-factor nonlinear agronomic response surfaces with
    genetic-algorithm or multistart parameter initialization, generalized nonlinear least
    squares, and expert Tier-3 surrogates including Gaussian processes, GAM/thin-plate
    smooths, random forests, neural networks, and one-step Bayesian optimization. Mixture
    experiments are deliberately outside scope. The core scientific API is independent of
    the optional Shiny interface.
